---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const SITE = 'https://dogtur.com';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Our Methodology | Dogtur"
  description="How Dogtur reviews senior dog products today — research-based reviews with attributed testing and review analysis — and our roadmap for hands-on testing."
  canonical={`${SITE}/methodology/`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Our methodology</h1>
    <p>
      Every product review on Dogtur is currently <strong>research-based</strong>.
      We have not yet completed hands-on testing of our own, so we say so
      plainly — and we never present anyone else's testing as ours. Each
      review is built from:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Gap analysis</strong> against the top-ranking reviews in the category, so we cover the subtopics readers actually need.</li>
      <li><strong>Attributed independent testing</strong> — when another publication has tested a product, we cite it by name and link to it. Their findings, their credit.</li>
      <li><strong>Verified owner-review analysis</strong> — patterns across real buyer reviews, described as review analysis, not as our own testing.</li>
      <li><strong>Specification and ingredient verification</strong> against manufacturer and retailer listings.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Our hands-on testing roadmap</h2>
    <p>
      Hands-on testing is where we're headed. When we get there, this is how
      we'll do it — no shortcuts:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Senior dogs first.</strong> Testers are aging dogs. A bed that works for a three-year-old athlete may fail a twelve-year-old with arthritis — we test for the dog the product is meant to serve.</li>
      <li><strong>Measured, not vibes.</strong> Foam compression, weight loads, temperature consistency, wash durability — we measure what we can and photograph the rest.</li>
      <li><strong>Real-world time.</strong> Products live with testers for days or weeks, not minutes. Sleep trials, daily walks, repeated washes.</li>
      <li><strong>No pay-to-play.</strong> Brands cannot pay for placement or a better score. Loaned products are disclosed; most test units are purchased retail.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What a review includes today</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Attribution:</strong> where each key finding comes from — whose test, whose review data.</li>
      <li><strong>Scorecard:</strong> the attributes that matter, scored from the evidence above.</li>
      <li><strong>Pros and cons</strong> drawn from research notes, not marketing copy.</li>
      <li><strong>Comparison table</strong> against the category's real alternatives.</li>
      <li><strong>Verdict:</strong> who it's for, who should skip it.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Once hands-on testing begins, reviews will gain a testing box — what we
      tested, for how long, with which dogs, dated — and this page will be
      updated to reflect it.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a test was wrong or a product changes, we re-test and update the
      review with a dated correction note. See the
      <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for our corrections process.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
